-- The voice of the robin. Bold, chatty and bossy in a cheerful way: the
-- neighbour who guards a patch of ground and regards the reader as part of
-- that patch. Brisk short sentences, orders, inspections and practical wit.
-- Sings nearly all year, at night too when a lamp is lit, follows anyone with
-- a spade for the worms, and is at their warmest in winter. Calls the reader
-- neighbour. The memories tell of a kettle, a brown year, a street lamp, an
-- old gardener's spade and a whistle of three notes.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

